  "pdf": "adc3544.pdf",
  "pages": "p.3-4 (pins; pin 18 NC, pin 19 FCLK), p.5 (ROC: AVDD, IOVDD 1.75-1.85 V), p.10 (SDR CMOS tPD 3-7 ns), p.11 (SPI SCLK 20 MHz, t(OD) 10.8 ns, t(ODZ) 14 ns max), p.37 (two's complement default), p.45 (default config Table 8-12: SDR CMOS, 2s complement), p.46-47 (24-bit SPI words), p.48-61 (register map)",
  "notModeled": [
    "analog input, references, auto-zero and clock biasing (the result is always the 0 V code 0x0000, two's complement)",
    "pipeline latency (1 clock cycle) is not modeled (the code is constant); data change tPD (7 ns max) after the sampling clock falling edge, DCLK follows the inverted clock",
    "CLKP/CLKM are a differential (or single-ended, 0.9 V centred) sampling clock: the model clocks on CLKP alone",
    "only the default output interface is modeled; the output interface/resolution registers (0x07, 0x1B, 0x39.., bit mapper, e-fuse load 0x13), DDR/serial CMOS 2-wire/1-wire modes, FCLK, DCLKIN and the CMOS output buffer power-down bits (0x0A-0x0C, 0x1F) do not change the outputs",
    "decimation filter, NCO, mixer (0x24-0x2D), test patterns (0x14-0x16) and offset-binary output (FORMAT, needs DIG BYP) do not change the output code",
    "PDN GLOBAL / PDN channel register bits and the PDN/SYNC pin used as SYNC (SYNC PIN EN) are stored only; the PDN/SYNC pin is modeled as power-down (blocks conversions, but the model also ignores the SPI bus while it is high)",
    "REFBUF pin voltage strapping of the reference / clock / interface (an analog level)",
    "R/W = 1 disables further register writes until the next write cycle (read-back mode); A[14:12] must be 0",
    "SPI is 3-wire: SDIO carries both directions (bus mosi and miso are the same pin); words beyond a multiple of 24 bits are ignored",
    "digital inputs RESET, PDN/SYNC, SCLK, SEN, SDIO are referred to AVDD (VIH 1.4-1.5 V); vcc is the IOVDD range (identical 1.75-1.85 V)",
    "output bit mapper range: the register map summary says 0x31..0x60, the register description 0x39..0x60, the mapping tables use addresses up to 0x72; modeled as 0x39..0x72",
    "timing: tOut is the SPI SDIO output delay t(OD) 10.8 ns max (the clocked data bus uses the same tOut; its real delay is tPD 3-7 ns after the clock falling edge)"
  ],
  "variants": "single-device datasheet; same register map as ADC354x without MASK REFSYS A, DLL PDN and AZ EN",
